# CASM WP38 trusted reference: casmorgexpl1
#
# Independently hand-assembled from the casmorgexpl1 fixture source in
# cmake/GenerateCasmTestFixtures.cmake (".ORG $3400" / "LDA #$01"). NOT
# produced by CASM. Was deliberately byte-identical to casmorg1.ref.hex
# (the same instruction with no .ORG at all) as WP38's own cross-check
# that implicit default-origin priming and an explicit .ORG at the same
# address produced exactly the same output. Cross-check:
#   - brain/plans/2026-07-24-casm-phase8-wp38-default-origin-and-static-override.md
#
# WP41 -- this equivalence was WP38-era and pre-R6 only. .ORG forces
# static mode, so casmorgexpl1 stays a plain PRG (unchanged by this WP);
# casmorg1 (implicit default, relocatable mode) gains a real R6 footer and
# is no longer byte-identical to this fixture. That divergence is the
# correct, intended outcome of R6 relocation existing at all, not a
# regression -- static and relocatable output are supposed to differ.
# Cross-check:
#   - brain/plans/2026-07-25-casm-phase8-wp41-r6-footer-serialization.md
#
# Source (.ORG $3400) and hand assembly:
#   00 34        PRG load-address header ($3400, little-endian)
#   A9 01        LDA #$01
#
# bytes: 4
# sha256: 52f7bcbf5b30fcc1fe893cc06d63dee077996d9e5d02f129b4a96e57c85eff8a

00 34
A9 01
